<title>UK: Betting seen on large UK Labour majority.</title>
<headline>Betting seen on large UK Labour majority.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sizeable betting has been seen on the main opposition Labour party winning a majority of at least 121 seats at the imminent general election, bookmakers Ladbrokes said on Friday.</p>
<p>Ladbrokes have cut the odds on such a majority to 6-1 from 8-1. A Labour majority of 81-100 is quoted at 8-1 and 61-80 at 6-1.</p>
<p>A Labour overall majority is quoted at 1-6 while the Conservative are rated a 3-1 chance. A hung parliament where no party has an overall majority is quoted at 7-2.</p>
<p>Odds</p>
<p>- Labour majority of 1-20 seats - 6-1;</p>
<p>21-40 seats - 3-1;</p>
<p>41-60 seats - 7-2;</p>
<p>61-80	 - 6-1;</p>
<p>81-100	- 8-1;</p>
<p>101-120     -14-1;</p>
<p>121 or more - 8-1.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
